+ * Command-mode panel (Pixel 1): send the frame. CTL0 START waits for the
+ * panel's TE and then streams the frame, up to ~32 ms in all; a START while
+ * that runs desyncs the panel's memory pointer (picture rolled, stripes,
+ * frozen until another full frame happens to land) and can survive a warm
+ * reset. So a START only goes out once the previous frame reported
+ * PING_PONG_0_DONE (MDP INTR_STATUS bit 8, latched without INTR_EN, as
+ * Linux mdss reads it), or 50 ms passed. Console kickoffs skip while a frame
